Here's the output:

```
{"Name":"john","Age":30}
```

And the full program (`Program.cs`):

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("john", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — a built-in policy available since .NET 9. It converts your lowercase parameter names (`name`, `age`) to PascalCase (`Name`, `Age`) in the JSON output, no custom code needed.
